- Fix the config in the captaind Docker image
  The config did not have all the required fields, so captaind did not start
  in the image or in the Docker Compose stack in `contrib/docker`. The config
  now has all the required fields and a bitcoind URL with the `http://`
  scheme. The Docker Compose stack now uses Bitcoin Core 32.1, because
  captaind requires v31 or later. The `cln` service in the stack now sets
  its hostname to `cln`, so captaind can verify the CLN TLS certificates.
  [#2805](https://gitlab.com/ark-bitcoin/bark/-/merge_requests/2805)
